---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <nav class="nav">
    <div class="nav-inner nav-inner-narrow">
      <a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">🐚</span> Conchquest</a>
      <a class="back" href="/">← Back to home</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="wrap page-wrap">
    <div class="draft-flag">
      <strong>Draft — not yet reviewed by an attorney.</strong> This template is written to reflect Conchquest's actual
      data flows (Supabase Auth, location logging, Cloudflare R2 photo storage, RevenueCat billing). Have a lawyer
      confirm it satisfies GDPR/CCPA and Apple/Google App Store requirements before publishing, and update it once
      analytics or ad providers are finalized.
    </div>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="updated">Draft prepared August 2026 · Not yet in effect</div>

    <h2>1. What this policy covers</h2>
    <p>This policy explains what data Conchquest collects, why, and how it's used, when you use our mobile app or website.</p>

    <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Why we collect it</th></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Account info</strong> (email, display name)</td><td>To create and secure your account, via Supabase Auth. Social login (Google/Apple) shares only what those providers permit.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Precise location</strong> (GPS)</td><td>To fetch tide, weather, and wave conditions for your current beach, and to let you log a find with coordinates.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Photos</strong></td><td>To attach images to shell finds you choose to log, stored via Cloudflare R2.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Find data</strong> (species, condition, notes, timestamp)</td><td>To build your personal shelling history and, if you choose to share it, contribute to the community find map.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Device and usage data</strong></td><td>To keep the app secure, diagnose crashes, and understand feature usage.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Subscription status</strong></td><td>Handled by Apple, Google, and RevenueCat to manage premium entitlements. We do not receive or store your payment card details.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>3. Location privacy controls</h2>
    <p>You control how your location is shared:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Private (default):</strong> your exact find location is visible only to you.</li>
      <li><strong>Approximate:</strong> a fuzzed, general area is shown to the community — never your exact coordinates.</li>
      <li><strong>Rare-find protection:</strong> finds tagged as rare species get additional location fuzzing to discourage over-collection of sensitive sites.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How we use your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To generate your personal Shelling Score and forecasts</li>
      <li>To operate the community find map and social features you opt into</li>
      <li>To send you notifications you've enabled (e.g., score-threshold alerts)</li>
      <li>To improve the accuracy of the Shelling Score using aggregated, anonymized community data</li>
      <li>To process subscription billing through Apple/Google and RevenueCat</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Third parties we work with</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Authentication</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cloudflare R2</td><td>Photo storage</td></tr>
      <tr><td>NOAA Tides &amp; Currents, OpenWeather</td><td>Environmental forecast data (we send them a location, not your identity)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>RevenueCat, Apple App Store, Google Play</td><td>Subscription billing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Firebase Cloud Messaging</td><td>Push notifications</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Railway</td><td>Backend hosting and database</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>

    <h2>6. Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Turn off location access at any time in your device settings (the Shelling Score will no longer auto-detect your beach)</li>
      <li>Delete individual finds or your entire account from Settings</li>
      <li>Request a copy or deletion of your data by contacting us below</li>
      <li>Opt out of push notifications at any time</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
    <p>We keep your account and find data until you delete your account. Deleted finds are removed from the community map immediately; backups are purged within 30 days.</p>

    <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>Conchquest is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we make material changes to how we handle your data, we'll notify you in-app before the changes take effect.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions, or want to exercise a data right? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@conchquest.com">privacy@conchquest.com</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <footer class="site-footer-simple">© 2026 Conchquest</footer>
</Layout>

<style>
  .nav-inner-narrow {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .page-wrap {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 56px 32px 100px;
  }
  .draft-flag {
    background: #fdf1ec;
    border: 1px solid #f3c9b8;
    color: #8a3819;
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #9b9a92;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  p,
  li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #3c3c39;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 8px 0 8px;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--teal-deep);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 16px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    color: #9b9a92;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
</style>
